  "commentary_text": "If no load capacitance is present, but a large input capacitance C , then the GS bandwidth is determined at the input. This is also true for many sensor and biomedical preamplifiers where the source resistance can be quite high (>1 MV). In this case, the BW is simply given by the RC product at the input. The GBW on the other hand, is not as simple as before. Many transistor parameters now play a role. Some of them can be bundled in the high-frequency parameter f . T For high-frequency performance, it is not sufficient however to make f large. Rather the T product f r must be optimized, which is a technological challenge indeed! T DS The channel length does not seem to play a role; both W and V −V must be made small!!! GS T All surprising results indeed!",
